WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.991
Launch week is noisy, and people decide in seconds.

2
00:00:04.041 --> 00:00:09.623
A short launch video gives everyone the same clear story, and your deck already holds most of it.

3
00:00:10.623 --> 00:00:14.301
Write the explanation carefully once, and it keeps working.

4
00:00:14.351 --> 00:00:18.958
A prospect can watch at 10pm, and a partner can forward it to their boss.

5
00:00:19.958 --> 00:00:21.430
Follow five beats.

6
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.877
Start with a problem viewers recognise, like chasing late invoices on Friday afternoons.

7
00:00:26.927 --> 00:00:31.476
Then show the product, how it works, the proof, and where to go next.

8
00:00:32.476 --> 00:00:34.192
Keep it shorter than you think.

9
00:00:34.242 --> 00:00:39.058
One to two minutes for product page and email, captioned clips for social.

10
00:00:39.108 --> 00:00:40.371
Thirty slides?

11
00:00:40.421 --> 00:00:41.975
Six to ten will do.

12
00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:45.550
Build it from your existing launch deck.

13
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:52.866
Cut internal slides and swap labels for claims: Reminders becomes, reminders go out on your schedule, not when you remember.

14
00:00:53.866 --> 00:00:56.035
Your speaker notes become the voiceover.

15
00:00:56.085 --> 00:01:01.005
On Pro, a.i. directs each animated scene, so the reveal feels produced.

16
00:01:01.055 --> 00:01:04.235
Try Basic first at powerpoint2vid.com.

